__d(function(e,t,a,o,i,n,s){i.exports=[{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>You can use the Settings to create up to two daily reminders set at times that make sense for you.</p> For instance, set them to your daily commute, so you can be reminded to use Mj\xf8lnir when you are travelling.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>Our &#8943; menu button at the top left corner of the flashcard screen allows you to undo immediately any scheduling action (including archiving cards).</p> You can also adjust the visual interface of the flashcards to fit your screen better.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>Our combination of content by frequency of use and spaced repetition is a bit like card-counting at the blackjack table.</p> You go from gambling about remembering notions of debatable usefulness to being certain that you'll know the ones that matter.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>Check out our social media and web presence at our Linktree: <a href='https://linktr.ee/mjolnirapp'>https://linktr.ee/mjolnirapp</a></p> In particular, look for our grammar cheat-sheet, where we have condensed the 30 most important grammar rules of the language, just make sure you zoom in!</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>Traditional language learning sometimes leaves the memorisation challenge to chance.</p>Instead, with Mj\xf8lnir you can easily define how many new notions you want to see every day, knowing that you'll see them in order of importance and learn what really matters first.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>When a card is shown with the veil, if you tap the upper part of it, only the answer will be shown.</p> This is useful if you don't want to be bothered by the explanation field, which is usually lengthier.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>At the moment, Mj\xf8lnir backs up your data on the cloud every time you complete a session fully by taking all the three counters to zero.</p> This is another reason to strive for consistency, so you don't risk losing progress.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>Mj\xf8lnir will probably require you to review cards from previous days almost every day.</p>However, you can use the Settings to select up to two days a week in which no new cards will be given to you, so you can rest a little.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>You might decide to archive cards the very first time they are shown to you, because you already know their content.</p>In this case, Mj\xf8lnir might add new cards to the session, to ensure that you keep yourself busy.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>Ever heard of that person who became good at something by not doing it? No? Neither have we!</p>Constant practice is a must for the acquisition of knowledge and skills. Self-discipline is hard, but we believe we have created an app that makes it as easy as it can be.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>If you ever skip using Mj\xf8lnir for a day, you'll have to make up for it.</p>The next day will in fact show you all the Reviews that belong to both the current day and the day (or days!) that you have skipped.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>Always try to pronounce your answers when studying.</p>This will help memorisation in general and, at the same time, will give you specific practice in articulating the sounds of the language.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>Take your time to learn new cards, but try to be quick with Reviews.</p>If remembering the answer takes you more than 2 or 3 seconds, be honest and go for <i>hard</i>.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>Take your sessions seriously!<br>Although Mj\xf8lnir is a great way to fill in idle time, your main session of the day will require you to focus.</p>Try to avoid distractions coming from either your smartphone or the surroundings.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>When you are working on verbs, nouns and adjectives, always consider the various forms.</p>Even if you get just one form wrong, you should consider the whole card to have been remembered incorrectly.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>Mj\xf8lnir is an excellent tool to learn grammar rules, single words and expressions.</p>However, nothing other than real conversations can expose you to the variety that the language can express.<br>So, make sure you practice real life conversations.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>Try and increase the situations that put you in contact with the language!</p>For example, try to change the language of your smartphone to Norwegian, to gain further exposure to the object of your studies.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>Try and be creative when it comes to memorisation. You could attach gestures or imagery to the words you are learning.</p>It's been proven that these \"memory associations\" can help you recollect more easily what you have been studying.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>If you find it easier to read Norwegian than to understand it spoken, keep expanding your vocabulary.</p>It can be easy to guess the meaning of a new word when reading it. When listening, however, you'll have no time to guess, so you'll need to know that word from before.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>The content of the B2 topics will tend to belong to specific topics and can't always be labelled as \"every day language\".</p>Because of this, the maximum interval and the streak needed for the check-in are longer, ensuring that these cards stay with you long enough.</div>"},{text:"<div class='tipOfTheDay'><p>The team behind Mj\xf8lnir would like to think of the Advanced section as something in continuous expansion.</p>If there is an important topic whose vocabulary you'd like to see in forthcoming topics, get in touch through the website and let us know!</div>"}]},2182,[]);
