rescheduled these 15 cards to come back for a review that will take place tomorrow or the day after tomorrow (unless you have archived them)."})]}),(0,y.jsxs)(n.View,{style:f.textWrap,children:[(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"4.  "}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:Object.assign({},f.text,{flex:1}),children:"On any of the following days, you will be given sets of 5 new cards from the next topics further down the list."})]}),(0,y.jsxs)(n.View,{style:f.textWrap,children:[(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"5.  "}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:Object.assign({},f.text,{flex:1}),children:"In the next days, you will also review any cards you have rescheduled in the previous days and that happen to have today as their due date."})]}),(0,y.jsxs)(n.View,{style:f.textWrap,children:[(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"6.  "}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:Object.assign({},f.text,{flex:1}),children:"If you keep on remembering the answers of your flashcards, you will be able to reschedule them to increasingly longer intervals."})]}),(0,y.jsxs)(n.View,{style:f.textWrap,children:[(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"7.  "}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:Object.assign({},f.text,{flex:1}),children:"However, if you admit to not remembering an answer, you should reschedule those flashcards to shorter intervals, which will mean more frequent practice of them."})]})]}),(0,y.jsxs)(n.View,{style:f.item,onLayout:function(e){return v(Object.assign({},b,{3:e.nativeEvent.layout.y}))},children:[(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.label,children:"I\u2019m done with my daily session, but why can\u2019t I study some more?"}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"Mj\xf8lnir\u2019s spaced repetition mechanism is built according to the way our brains actually work. Because of this, it\u2019s very important to review a card when it\u2019s due, in order to reinforce your learning efficiently, just at the right time."}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"After a few days, your daily session will grow into the size/length you have chosen, which is given by the number of new cards and of reviews for that day. Now, you might have the time to study some more on a given day, but you\u2019ll have to be able to tackle this increase on future days too, which might be difficult for you to manage."}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"For this reason, we recommend trying to focus on a smaller but consistently achievable workload."}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"However, each session will offer to add 5 more new flashcards at some point, should you really want to, and we are working on an additional study mode offering more flexibility."})]}),(0,y.jsxs)(n.View,{style:f.item,onLayout:function(e){return v(Object.assign({},b,{4:e.nativeEvent.layout.y}))},children:[(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.label,children:"Will my session grow to a huge number of reviews?"}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"The number of reviews from previous days will grow for a while, but then should remain stable, because you won\u2019t be studying a certain flashcard forever. Some cards, in fact, will leave your study routine and be archived because:"}),(0,y.jsxs)(n.View,{style:f.textWrap,children:[(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"a.  "}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:Object.assign({},f.text,{flex:1}),children:"you decide to archive that card manually"})]}),(0,y.jsxs)(n.View,{style:f.textWrap,children:[(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"b.  "}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:Object.assign({},f.text,{flex:1}),children:"you\u2019ll have rescheduled it correctly a certain number of times in a row once the card has reached its longest possible interval, and another \u201cEasy\u201d rescheduling will cause it to archive"})]}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"Remember that the 3000+ vocabulary items of Mj\xf8lnir represent about 95% of every day\u2019s language. This means that by just using your Scandinavian language every day, you will practice a lot of what you have learned."}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"Also, the first few hundreds of items (i.e. A1 and parts of A2) are so fundamental to the language that the intermediate and advanced examples will necessarily use them, helping you keep them fresh in your memory."})]}),(0,y.jsxs)(n.View,{style:f.item,onLayout:function(e){return v(Object.assign({},b,{5:e.nativeEvent.layout.y}))},children:[(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.label,children:"I know I won\u2019t be able to study for a while, can I pause Mj\xf8lnir so that I won\u2019t have a backlog of many days?"}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"You can\u2019t pause Mj\xf8lnir because you can\u2019t pause your own forgetting. Sadly, allowing to pause would go against the very logic of spaced repetition."}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"In other words, just like you can\u2019t avoid your body losing fitness if you stop exercising for long enough, you can\u2019t stop your recollection of a given notion being at risk of degrading if you stop reviewing it at the scheduled intervals for long enough. It\u2019s physiological."}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"And even if we allowed the app to pause, this wouldn\u2019t magically stop you from likely forgetting those notions: it would just give you a false sense of being up-to-date, when you are not. This means that if you were to start again on this hypothetically paused schedule, you\u2019d have to admit to not remembering most of the reviews, which would almost certainly create a backlog anyway."}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"Therefore, if you end up with a few days\u2019 worth of backlog, the best approach is to simply catch up with it over a number of days. The app will always show you first the review cards on a shorter interval, which are likely the more urgent ones, because these notions are new and your recollection of them is likely weak. Anything on an interval of 10 days or longer can easily be post-poned by a couple of days without major systematic repercussions on your likelihood of recollecting it."}),(0,y.jsx)(n.Text,{style:f.text,children:"Simply, do not worry about the backlog: just work through it as you can manage. Other than the backlog itself, there is no punishment or penalty for it, so don\u2019t worry about it. If you want further assistance, please get in touch with customer support."})]})]})]})})})},2187,[1,56,77,892,5,944,990,1252,1406,1243,1435,80]);
